IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea-core`
IMPORT `ea-definitions`

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 5/12/2025" -- LAYER 1, PART 2 (a): ss 8 to 17, from illegal
-- terms to the right to join a trade union.
--
-- Source text: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore
-- Statutes Online (inputs/EmA1968.txt).  It is not the official text.  Every
-- `-- src:` line copies a line of that file (script-generated); every quotation in
-- a FALSE-kind or NOTHING-kind comment is a phrase of it (checked by a script).
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its
-- own words.  NOTHING means the Act does not answer on these facts and is never to
-- be read as no.  Each branch that answers no carries "FALSE-kind", each that
-- answers "not covered" carries "NOTHING-kind", and "marginal (a)" or "marginal (b)"
-- marks the branches that rest on one of the two readings for a lawyer
-- (NOTES.md, Marginal readings for a lawyer (ea1)).
-- Money is a NUMBER of Singapore dollars; a count of days is a NUMBER; a calendar
-- day is `Date day month year`.

§ `Employment Act 1968 -- Part 2 Contracts of service, ss 8 to 17`

§§ `s 8 Illegal terms of contract of service`

-- src:791 | 8. Every term of a contract of service which provides a condition of
-- src:792 | service which is less favourable to an employee than any of the
-- src:793 | conditions of service prescribed by this Act is illegal and void to the
-- src:794 | extent that it is so less favourable.
@ref s 8 (src:791-794)
GIVEN `the term is a term of a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the term provides a condition of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition is less favourable to an employee than a condition of service prescribed by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8 the term is illegal and void to the extent that it is so less favourable` MEANS
    IF `the term is a term of a contract of service` AND `the term provides a condition of service` AND `the condition is less favourable to an employee than a condition of service prescribed by this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 8 says what is illegal and void and does not say that a term which is not less favourable is valid
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 9 Termination of contract`

-- src:798 | 9.—(1) A contract of service for a specified piece of work or for a
-- src:799 | specified period of time, unless otherwise terminated in accordance
-- src:800 | with the provisions of this Part, terminates when the work specified in
-- src:801 | the contract is completed or the period of time for which the contract
-- src:802 | was made has expired.
@ref s 9(1) (src:798-802)
GIVEN `the contract of service is for a specified piece of work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work specified in the contract has been completed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract of service is for a specified period of time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of time for which the contract was made has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract of service was otherwise terminated in accordance with the provisions of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(1) the contract of service terminates when the work is completed or the period has expired` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless otherwise terminated in accordance with the provisions of this Part" -- marginal (a)
        IF `the contract of service was otherwise terminated in accordance with the provisions of this Part` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF (`the contract of service is for a specified piece of work` AND `the work specified in the contract has been completed`) OR (`the contract of service is for a specified period of time` AND `the period of time for which the contract was made has expired`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) speaks only of "A contract of service for a specified piece of work or for a specified period of time" (scope limit, ruled 2026-11-05 (c))
        IF (NOT `the contract of service is for a specified piece of work`) AND (NOT `the contract of service is for a specified period of time`) THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "terminates when the work specified in the contract is completed or the period of time for which the contract was made has expired" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): "when" counts as "where", and neither has happened
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:804 | (2) A contract of service for an unspecified period of time is
-- src:805 | deemed to run until terminated by either party in accordance with the
-- src:806 | provisions of this Part.
@ref s 9(2) (src:804-806)
GIVEN `the contract of service is for an unspecified period of time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `either party has terminated it in accordance with the provisions of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(2) the contract of service is deemed to run` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2) speaks only of a contract of service for an unspecified period of time
        IF NOT `the contract of service is for an unspecified period of time` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "deemed to run until terminated by either party in accordance with the provisions of this Part" -- marginal (a)
        IF `either party has terminated it in accordance with the provisions of this Part` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 10 Notice of termination of contract`

-- src:810 | 10.—(1) Either party to a contract of service may at any time give to
-- src:811 | the other party notice of the firstmentioned party’s intention to
-- src:812 | terminate the contract of service.
@ref s 10(1) (src:810-812)
GIVEN `the person is a party to a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(1) the party may at any time give the other party notice of intention to terminate the contract of service` MEANS
    IF `the person is a party to a contract of service`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (1) speaks only of a party to a contract of service
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The text gives the length of the notice by the contract if it provides one, and
-- otherwise by subsection (3).  Reading A (taken here): the contract governs.  The
-- s 8 reading, in which a shorter contract term is void, is the separate function
-- after subsection (3) below (NOTES.md, fork F-10(2)).
-- src:814 | (2) The length of the notice must be the same for both employer and
-- src:815 | employee and is to be determined by any provision made for the
-- src:816 | notice in the terms of the contract of service, or, in the absence of such
-- src:817 | provision, must be in accordance with subsection (3).
@ref s 10(2) (src:814-817)
GIVEN `the length of the notice that the terms of the contract of service provide, in days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the least number of days of notice under subsection (3)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 10(2) the length of the notice, in days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the length of the notice that the terms of the contract of service provide, in days`
    WHEN JUST days THEN JUST days
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the contract makes no provision the length "must be in accordance with subsection (3)", and that is subsection (3)'s answer, which may be none
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the least number of days of notice under subsection (3)`

@ref s 10(2) (src:814-817)
GIVEN `the length of the notice for the employer, in days` IS A NUMBER
      `the length of the notice for the employee, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10(2) the length of the notice is the same for both employer and employee` MEANS
    `the length of the notice for the employer, in days` EQUALS `the length of the notice for the employee, in days`

-- The weeks and years of subsection (3) are counted from the day the employment
-- began: 26 weeks is 182 days after that day, and a year is the same day of the
-- month in a later year (NOTES.md, fork F-10(3)).  "So employed" is measured at the
-- day the notice is given.
-- src:819 | (3) The notice to terminate the service of a person who is employed
-- src:820 | under a contract of service must be at least —
-- src:822 | (a) one day’s notice if the person has been so employed for less
-- src:823 | than 26 weeks;
-- src:825 | (b) one week’s notice if the person has been so employed for
-- src:826 | 26 weeks or more but less than 2 years;
-- src:828 | (c) 2 weeks’ notice if the person has been so employed for
-- src:829 | 2 years or more but less than 5 years; and
-- src:834 | (d) 4 weeks’ notice if the person has been so employed for
-- src:835 | 5 years or more.
@ref s 10(3) (src:819-835)
GIVEN employment IS A `Dates of the employment`
      `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE
      `the person is employed under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 10(3) the least number of days of notice` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (3) speaks only of the notice to terminate the service of a person who is employed under a contract of service
        IF NOT `the person is employed under a contract of service` THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a notice given before the employment began is not one the subsection speaks of
        IF (`the day the notice is given` LESS THAN began) THEN NOTHING
        -- (a) "one day’s notice if the person has been so employed for less than 26 weeks"
        IF (`days employed` LESS THAN 182) THEN JUST 1
        -- (b) "one week’s notice if the person has been so employed for 26 weeks or more but less than 2 years"
        IF (`the day the notice is given` LESS THAN `the day the employment reaches 2 years`) THEN JUST 7
        -- (c) "2 weeks’ notice if the person has been so employed for 2 years or more but less than 5 years"
        IF (`the day the notice is given` LESS THAN `the day the employment reaches 5 years`) THEN JUST 14
        -- (d) "4 weeks’ notice if the person has been so employed for 5 years or more"
        OTHERWISE JUST 28
    WHERE
        began MEANS employment's `began on`
        `days employed` MEANS (Day `the day the notice is given`) MINUS (Day began)
        `the day the employment reaches 2 years` MEANS Date (DATE_DAY began) (DATE_MONTH began) ((DATE_YEAR began) PLUS 2)
        `the day the employment reaches 5 years` MEANS Date (DATE_DAY began) (DATE_MONTH began) ((DATE_YEAR began) PLUS 5)

-- Section 8 applied to a notice term: a contract term shorter than the least notice
-- of subsection (3) is a condition less favourable to the employee than one the Act
-- prescribes, if the shorter notice is the less favourable to the employee.
-- src:791 | 8. Every term of a contract of service which provides a condition of
-- src:792 | service which is less favourable to an employee than any of the
-- src:793 | conditions of service prescribed by this Act is illegal and void to the
-- src:794 | extent that it is so less favourable.
@ref s 8 (src:791-794)
GIVEN `the length of the notice that the terms of the contract of service provide, in days` IS A NUMBER
      `the least number of days of notice under subsection (3)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the shorter notice is less favourable to the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 8 the number of days by which the contract's term on the length of notice is void as shorter than section 10(3)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the least number of days of notice under subsection (3)`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the comparison needs the least notice of section 10(3), which may be none
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST least THEN
        IF `the shorter notice is less favourable to the employee` AND (`the length of the notice that the terms of the contract of service provide, in days` LESS THAN least)
        THEN JUST (least MINUS `the length of the notice that the terms of the contract of service provide, in days`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 8 voids a term only "to the extent that it is so less favourable" and says nothing of a term that is not
        ELSE NOTHING

-- src:837 | (4) This section does not prevent either party from waiving that
-- src:838 | party’s right to notice on any occasion.
@ref s 10(4) (src:837-838)
GIVEN `the right to notice waived is the waiving party's own` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(4) the party may waive the party's right to notice` MEANS
    IF `the right to notice waived is the waiving party's own`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "waiving that party’s right to notice" speaks of a party's own right
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:840 | (5) The notice must be written and may be given at any time, and
-- src:841 | the day on which the notice is given is included in the period of the
-- src:842 | notice.
@ref s 10(5) (src:840-842)
GIVEN notice IS A `Notice of termination`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(5) the notice is written` MEANS
    IF notice's `in writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must be written" -- a notice that is not written does not meet it; the function answers whether the notice is written and is kept under that name (it says nothing of what follows)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref s 10(5) (src:840-842)
GIVEN `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(5) the notice may be given on the day` MEANS
    -- "may be given at any time": the subsection sets no limit on the day, so every day answers JUST TRUE
    JUST TRUE

@ref s 10(5) (src:840-842)
GIVEN `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE
      `the length of the notice, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 10(5) the last day of the period of the notice` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a notice of no days has no last day
        IF `the length of the notice, in days` LESS THAN 1 THEN NOTHING
        -- "the day on which the notice is given is included in the period of the notice"
        OTHERWISE JUST (Date ((Day `the day the notice is given`) PLUS (`the length of the notice, in days` MINUS 1)))

§§ `s 11 Termination of contract without notice`

-- src:846 | 11.—(1) Either party to a contract of service may terminate the
-- src:847 | contract of service without notice or, if notice has already been given
-- src:848 | in accordance with section 10, without waiting for the expiry of that
-- src:849 | notice, by paying to the other party a sum equal to the amount of
-- src:850 | salary at the gross rate of pay which would have accrued to the
-- src:851 | employee during the period of the notice and in the case of a
-- src:852 | monthly‑rated employee where the period of the notice is less than a
-- src:853 | month, the amount payable for any one day is the gross rate of pay for
-- src:854 | one day’s work.
@ref s 11(1) (src:846-854)
GIVEN `the party pays the other party the sum that subsection (1) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(1) the party may terminate the contract of service without notice, or without waiting for the notice to expire` MEANS
    IF `the party pays the other party the sum that subsection (1) requires`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by paying to the other party a sum equal to the amount of salary at the gross rate of pay"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "Less than a month" is a calendar month (Interpretation Act 1965 s 2(1), staged in
-- DEPENDENCIES): a period of N days starting on the day of notice is less than a
-- month if it ends before the same day of the next month; where the next month has no
-- such day (a notice on the 31st), the month is taken to end on the next month's last day
-- (NOTES.md, fork F-11(1)).
@ref s 11(1) (src:846-854)
GIVEN `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE
      `the length of the notice, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11(1) the period of the notice is less than a month` MEANS
    (Day `the day the notice is given`) PLUS `the length of the notice, in days` LESS THAN (Day `the first day after the month`)
    WHERE
        `the same day of the next month` MEANS Date (DATE_DAY `the day the notice is given`) ((DATE_MONTH `the day the notice is given`) PLUS 1) (DATE_YEAR `the day the notice is given`)
        `the first of the month after the next` MEANS Date 1 ((DATE_MONTH `the day the notice is given`) PLUS 2) (DATE_YEAR `the day the notice is given`)
        `the first day after the month` MEANS IF `the same day of the next month` LESS THAN `the first of the month after the next` THEN `the same day of the next month` ELSE `the first of the month after the next`

-- The sum is the salary at the gross rate of pay that would have accrued during the
-- period of the notice; for a monthly-rated employee and a period shorter than a
-- month it is the gross rate of pay for one day's work (the Third Schedule's
-- answer, taken as an input: seam S6) for each day.  Reading: "the period of the
-- notice" is the whole period (NOTES.md, fork F-11(1)).
@ref s 11(1) (src:846-854)
GIVEN `the salary at the gross rate of pay that would have accrued during the period of the notice` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the employee is monthly-rated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of the notice is less than a month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days in the period of the notice` IS A NUMBER
      `the answer of sch 3 gross rate of pay per day` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 11(1) the sum payable by the party who terminates` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the employee is monthly-rated` AND `the period of the notice is less than a month` THEN
            CONSIDER `the answer of sch 3 gross rate of pay per day`
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the gross rate of pay for one day's work is the Third Schedule's answer, which may be none
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST rate THEN JUST (rate TIMES `the number of days in the period of the notice`)
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): for any other employee the sum is the salary at the gross rate of pay that would have accrued, which the caller states
        OTHERWISE `the salary at the gross rate of pay that would have accrued during the period of the notice`

-- src:856 | (2) Either party to a contract of service may terminate the contract
-- src:857 | of service without notice in the event of any wilful breach by the other
-- src:858 | party of a condition of the contract of service.
@ref s 11(2) (src:856-858)
GIVEN `the other party has wilfully breached a condition of the contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(2) the party may terminate the contract of service without notice` MEANS
    IF `the other party has wilfully breached a condition of the contract of service`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the event of any wilful breach by the other party of a condition of the contract of service" -- "in the event of" read as "where" (assumed, not ruled: fork F-EVENT); ruled 2026-11-05 (b)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 12 Contractual age`

-- src:862 | 12.—(1) Despite any other written law, a person below 18 years of
-- src:863 | age is, subject to the provisions of this Act, competent to enter into a
-- src:864 | contract of service.
@ref s 12(1) (src:862-864)
GIVEN `age in completed years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(1) the person is competent to enter into a contract of service` MEANS
    IF `age in completed years` LESS THAN 18
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) speaks of "a person below 18 years of age"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:866 | (2) No contract of service as an employee is enforceable against a
-- src:867 | person below 18 years of age and no damages or indemnity are
-- src:868 | recoverable from that person in respect of the contract of service
-- src:869 | unless it is for his or her benefit.
@ref s 12(2) (src:866-869)
GIVEN `age in completed years` IS A NUMBER
      `the contract of service is for the benefit of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2) the contract of service as an employee is enforceable against the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No contract of service as an employee is enforceable against a person below 18 years of age" -- marginal (a)
        IF (`age in completed years` LESS THAN 18) AND (NOT `the contract of service is for the benefit of the person`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless it is for his or her benefit", and the subsection speaks only of a person below 18 years of age
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 12(2) (src:866-869)
GIVEN `age in completed years` IS A NUMBER
      `the contract of service is for the benefit of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2) damages or indemnity are recoverable from the person in respect of the contract of service` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no damages or indemnity are recoverable from that person in respect of the contract of service" -- marginal (a)
        IF (`age in completed years` LESS THAN 18) AND (NOT `the contract of service is for the benefit of the person`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless it is for his or her benefit", and the subsection speaks only of a person below 18 years of age
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- The bar of subsection (2) as a yes/no question of its own (ruled 2026-11-05, the
-- bar rule): JUST TRUE while the bar applies, JUST FALSE once the text lifts it
-- ("unless it is for his or her benefit"), NOTHING outside the age the subsection
-- speaks of.  Whether the contract IS enforceable is the function above.
@ref s 12(2) (src:866-869)
GIVEN `age in completed years` IS A NUMBER
      `the contract of service is for the benefit of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2) the bar on enforcing the contract of service as an employee against the person applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) speaks of "a person below 18 years of age" (scope limit with no "only", ruled 2026-11-05 (c))
        IF NOT (`age in completed years` LESS THAN 18) THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it is for his or her benefit" -- the text lifts the bar
        IF `the contract of service is for the benefit of the person` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
@ref s 12(2) (src:866-869)
GIVEN `age in completed years` IS A NUMBER
      `the contract of service is for the benefit of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2) the bar on recovering damages or indemnity from the person in respect of the contract of service applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) speaks of "a person below 18 years of age" (scope limit with no "only", ruled 2026-11-05 (c))
        IF NOT (`age in completed years` LESS THAN 18) THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it is for his or her benefit" -- the text lifts the bar
        IF `the contract of service is for the benefit of the person` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
§§ `s 13 When contract deemed to be broken by employer and employee`

-- src:874 | 13.—(1) An employer is deemed to have broken the employer’s
-- src:875 | contract of service with the employee if the employer fails to pay
-- src:876 | salary in accordance with Part 3.
@ref s 13(1) (src:874-876)
GIVEN `the employer fails to pay salary in accordance with Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13(1) the employer is deemed to have broken the employer's contract of service with the employee` MEANS
    IF `the employer fails to pay salary in accordance with Part 3`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the employer fails to pay salary in accordance with Part 3" -- marginal (a)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:881 | (2) An employee is deemed to have broken the employee’s contract
-- src:882 | of service with the employer if the employee is absent from work for
-- src:883 | more than 2 days continuously without prior leave from the employer
-- src:884 | and —
-- src:886 | (a) the employee has no reasonable excuse for the absence; or
-- src:888 | (b) the employee does not inform and does not attempt to
-- src:889 | inform the employer of the excuse for the absence.
@ref s 13(2) (src:881-889)
GIVEN `the number of days the employee is continuously absent from work` IS A NUMBER
      `the employee has prior leave from the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee has a reasonable excuse for the absence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee informs or attempts to inform the employer of the excuse for the absence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13(2) the employee is deemed to have broken the employee's contract of service with the employer` MEANS
    IF (`the number of days the employee is continuously absent from work` GREATER THAN 2)
       AND (NOT `the employee has prior leave from the employer`)
       AND ((NOT `the employee has a reasonable excuse for the absence`) OR (NOT `the employee informs or attempts to inform the employer of the excuse for the absence`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the employee is absent from work for more than 2 days continuously without prior leave from the employer and" -- marginal (a)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 14 Dismissal`

-- src:895 | 14.—(1) An employer may after due inquiry dismiss without notice
-- src:896 | an employee employed by the employer on the grounds of
-- src:897 | misconduct inconsistent with the fulfilment of the express or
-- src:898 | implied conditions of the employee’s service, except that instead of
-- src:899 | dismissing an employee an employer may —
-- src:901 | (a) instantly down-grade the employee; or
-- src:903 | (b) instantly suspend the employee from work without
-- src:904 | payment of salary for a period not exceeding one week.
@ref s 14(1) (src:895-904)
GIVEN ground IS A `Ground of dismissal`
      `the employer held a due inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(1) the employer may dismiss the employee without notice` MEANS
    IF (ground EQUALS `Ground: misconduct inconsistent with the fulfilment of the conditions of service`) AND `the employer held a due inquiry`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "after due inquiry dismiss without notice an employee ... on the grounds of misconduct inconsistent with the fulfilment of the express or implied conditions of the employee’s service"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:901 | (a) instantly down-grade the employee; or
@ref s 14(1)(a) (src:901-901)
GIVEN ground IS A `Ground of dismissal`
      `the employer held a due inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(1)(a) the employer may instantly down-grade the employee instead of dismissing the employee` MEANS
    IF (ground EQUALS `Ground: misconduct inconsistent with the fulfilment of the conditions of service`) AND `the employer held a due inquiry`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except that instead of dismissing an employee an employer may" speaks of the case in which the employer may dismiss on the ground of misconduct after due inquiry
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:903 | (b) instantly suspend the employee from work without
-- src:904 | payment of salary for a period not exceeding one week.
@ref s 14(1)(b) (src:903-904)
GIVEN ground IS A `Ground of dismissal`
      `the employer held a due inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days the employee is suspended without payment of salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(1)(b) the employer may instantly suspend the employee from work without payment of salary instead of dismissing the employee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the permission is "instead of dismissing", so it exists only where the employer may "after due inquiry dismiss without notice" for misconduct (scope limit, ruled 2026-11-05 (c))
        IF NOT ((ground EQUALS `Ground: misconduct inconsistent with the fulfilment of the conditions of service`) AND `the employer held a due inquiry`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `the number of days the employee is suspended without payment of salary` AT MOST 7 THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period not exceeding one week" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): outside the period fixed in the text's own words
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- Section 3 of the Employment Claims Act 2016 is not among the sources: the caller
-- states whether it leaves the claim open (a MAYBE BOOLEAN, so a NOTHING is carried on).
-- src:908 | (2) Despite subsection (1), but subject to section 3 of the
-- src:909 | Employment Claims Act 2016, where a relevant employee
-- src:910 | considers that he or she has been dismissed without just cause or
-- src:911 | excuse by his or her employer, the employee may lodge a claim,
-- src:912 | under section 13 of that Act, for either of the following remedies:
-- src:914 | (a) reinstatement in the employee’s former employment;
-- src:916 | (b) compensation.
@ref s 14(2) (src:908-916)
GIVEN dismissal IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 14(2A) the employee is a relevant employee` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the employee considers that he or she has been dismissed without just cause or excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 3 of the Employment Claims Act 2016 leaves the claim open` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      relief IS A `Relief a claimant may seek`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(2) the employee may lodge a claim under section 13 of the Employment Claims Act 2016 for the remedy` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a relevant employee considers that he or she has been dismissed without just cause or excuse" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): the employee does not consider it
        IF NOT `the employee considers that he or she has been dismissed without just cause or excuse` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a relevant employee considers that he or she has been dismissed without just cause or excuse" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): there was no dismissal, or the employee is not a relevant employee under subsection (2A)
        IF (dismissal EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`the answer of s 14(2A) the employee is a relevant employee` EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the subsection is "subject to section 3 of the Employment Claims Act 2016", which is not among the sources
        IF (`section 3 of the Employment Claims Act 2016 leaves the claim open` EQUALS NOTHING) THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the ending was a dismissal comes from the definition of "dismiss", which may give none
        IF (dismissal EQUALS NOTHING) THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the employee is a relevant employee comes from subsection (2A), which may give none
        IF (`the answer of s 14(2A) the employee is a relevant employee` EQUALS NOTHING) THEN NOTHING
        IF (`section 3 of the Employment Claims Act 2016 leaves the claim open` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND ((relief EQUALS `Relief: reinstatement in the former employment`) OR (relief EQUALS `Relief: compensation`)) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to section 3 of the Employment Claims Act 2016" -- the conditions of the "where" are met and section 3 does not leave the claim open, or the remedy is not one of "either of the following remedies" (scope limit with no "only", ruled 2026-11-05 (c))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- The converter lost the nesting of subsection (2A) at a page break and restarted
-- the lettering at line 934: "(a) after having served that employer for at least 6
-- months in any position ..." is the tail of limb (a), not a new limb (a) (NOTES.md,
-- fork F-14(2A)).
DECLARE `s 14(2A) Manner of dismissal` IS ONE OF
    `s 14(2A) dismissed with notice`
    `s 14(2A) dismissed without notice but with payment of any salary in lieu of notice`
    `s 14(2A) dismissed without notice and without salary in lieu of such notice`

-- src:920 | (2A) For the purposes of subsection (2), a relevant employee
-- src:921 | means —
-- src:923 | (a) an employee employed in a managerial or an executive
-- src:924 | position —
-- src:926 | (i) who is dismissed with notice; or
-- src:928 | (ii) who is dismissed without notice but receives
-- src:929 | payment of any salary in lieu of notice,
-- src:934 | (a) after having served that employer for at least 6 months in
-- src:935 | any position (whether or not a managerial or an executive
-- src:936 | position);
-- src:938 | (b) an employee employed in a managerial or an executive
-- src:939 | position who is dismissed without notice and without
-- src:940 | salary in lieu of such notice; or
-- src:942 | (c) an employee not employed in a managerial or an executive
-- src:943 | position.
@ref s 14(2A) (src:920-943)
GIVEN `the employee is employed in a managerial or an executive position` IS A BOOLEAN
      manner IS A `s 14(2A) Manner of dismissal`
      `the number of complete months the employee has served that employer in any position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(2A) the employee is a relevant employee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- (a) a managerial or executive employee dismissed with notice, or without notice but with salary in lieu, after at least 6 months' service in any position
        IF `the employee is employed in a managerial or an executive position` AND ((manner EQUALS `s 14(2A) dismissed with notice`) OR (manner EQUALS `s 14(2A) dismissed without notice but with payment of any salary in lieu of notice`)) AND (`the number of complete months the employee has served that employer in any position` AT LEAST 6) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- (b) a managerial or executive employee dismissed without notice and without salary in lieu
        IF `the employee is employed in a managerial or an executive position` AND (manner EQUALS `s 14(2A) dismissed without notice and without salary in lieu of such notice`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- (c) an employee not employed in a managerial or an executive position
        IF NOT `the employee is employed in a managerial or an executive position` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a relevant employee means"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- The Tribunal is the body of s 2(1) "Tribunal"; its answer is taken as an input.
-- src:947 | (3) If a Tribunal hearing the claim is satisfied that the employee has
-- src:948 | been dismissed without just cause or excuse, the Tribunal may,
-- src:949 | despite any rule of law or agreement to the contrary —
-- src:951 | (a) in a claim for reinstatement of the employee in his or her
-- src:952 | former employment, direct the employer —
-- src:954 | (i) to reinstate the employee in the employee’s former
-- src:955 | employment; and
-- src:957 | (ii) to pay the employee an amount equivalent to the
-- src:958 | wages that the employee would have earned, if the
-- src:959 | employee had not been dismissed; or
-- src:961 | (b) in a claim for compensation, direct the employer to pay, as
-- src:962 | compensation to the employee, an amount of wages
-- src:963 | determined by the Tribunal.
@ref s 14(3) (src:947-963)
GIVEN `the body hearing the claim is the Tribunal` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Tribunal is satisfied that the employee has been dismissed without just cause or excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      relief IS A `Relief a claimant may seek`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(3)(a) the Tribunal may direct the employer to reinstate the employee and to pay the wages the employee would have earned` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the body is the Tribunal comes from the definition of "Tribunal", which may give none
        IF (`the body hearing the claim is the Tribunal` EQUALS NOTHING) THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a Tribunal hearing the claim is satisfied that the employee has been dismissed without just cause or excuse" -- an unmet "if" (or the body is not a Tribunal)
        IF (`the body hearing the claim is the Tribunal` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (NOT `the Tribunal is satisfied that the employee has been dismissed without just cause or excuse`) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF relief EQUALS `Relief: reinstatement in the former employment` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in a claim for reinstatement of the employee in his or her former employment" -- the claim is for another remedy (scope limit, ruled 2026-11-05 (c))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 14(3)(b) (src:961-963)
GIVEN `the body hearing the claim is the Tribunal` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Tribunal is satisfied that the employee has been dismissed without just cause or excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      relief IS A `Relief a claimant may seek`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(3)(b) the Tribunal may direct the employer to pay compensation, an amount of wages determined by the Tribunal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the body is the Tribunal comes from the definition of "Tribunal", which may give none
        IF (`the body hearing the claim is the Tribunal` EQUALS NOTHING) THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a Tribunal hearing the claim is satisfied that the employee has been dismissed without just cause or excuse" -- an unmet "if" (or the body is not a Tribunal)
        IF (`the body hearing the claim is the Tribunal` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (NOT `the Tribunal is satisfied that the employee has been dismissed without just cause or excuse`) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF relief EQUALS `Relief: compensation` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in a claim for compensation" -- the claim is for another remedy (scope limit, ruled 2026-11-05 (c))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:977 | (8) For the purposes of an inquiry under subsection (1), the
-- src:978 | employer —
-- src:980 | (a) may suspend the employee from work for —
-- src:982 | (i) a period not exceeding one week; or
-- src:987 | (ii) such longer period as the Commissioner may
-- src:988 | determine on an application by the employer; but
@ref s 14(8)(a) (src:977-988)
GIVEN `the number of days the employee is suspended from work` IS A NUMBER
      `the longer period, in days, that the Commissioner has determined on the employer's application` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(8)(a) the employer may suspend the employee from work for the period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the number of days the employee is suspended from work` AT MOST 7) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the Commissioner has determined a longer period and the suspension does not exceed it` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a period not exceeding one week; or" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (a): outside the period fixed in the text's own words, and no longer period the Commissioner determined covers it
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the Commissioner has determined a longer period and the suspension does not exceed it` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the longer period, in days, that the Commissioner has determined on the employer's application`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST longer THEN `the number of days the employee is suspended from work` AT MOST longer

-- src:990 | (b) must pay the employee at least half the employee’s salary
-- src:991 | during the period the employee is suspended from work.
@ref s 14(8)(b) (src:990-991)
GIVEN `the employee's salary for the period of the suspension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 14(8)(b) the least the employer must pay the employee during the suspension` MEANS
    `the employee's salary for the period of the suspension` DIVIDED BY 2

-- src:995 | (9) If the inquiry does not disclose any misconduct on the
-- src:996 | employee’s part, the employer must immediately restore to the
-- src:997 | employee the full amount of the salary so withheld.
@ref s 14(9) (src:995-997)
GIVEN `the inquiry discloses misconduct on the employee's part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(9) the employer must immediately restore the full amount of the salary withheld` MEANS
    IF NOT `the inquiry discloses misconduct on the employee's part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the inquiry does not disclose any misconduct on the employee’s part" -- marginal (a)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref s 14(9) (src:995-997)
GIVEN `the inquiry discloses misconduct on the employee's part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the salary withheld` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 14(9) the amount the employer must restore` MEANS
    IF NOT `the inquiry discloses misconduct on the employee's part`
    THEN JUST `the salary withheld`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the inquiry does not disclose any misconduct" -- the subsection states no amount for the other case (a number has no "no": marginal (a) would read it as 0)
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 14(9) Actor` IS ONE OF
    `s 14(9) the employer`

DECLARE `s 14(9) Action` IS ONE OF
    `s 14(9) restore to the employee the full amount of the salary withheld`

-- The duty of subsection (9) as a regulative rule: "immediately" is no days.
@ref s 14(9) (src:995-997)
GIVEN `the inquiry discloses misconduct on the employee's part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 14(9) Actor` `s 14(9) Action`
`s 14(9) the employer's duty to restore the salary` MEANS
    IF NOT `the inquiry discloses misconduct on the employee's part`
    THEN PARTY `s 14(9) the employer`
         MUST `s 14(9) restore to the employee the full amount of the salary withheld`
         WITHIN 0
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `s 14(9) the employer` BECAUSE "the employer did not immediately restore the full amount of the salary withheld"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `s 15 Termination by employee threatened by danger`

-- src:1001 | 15. An employee may terminate his or her contract of service with
-- src:1002 | his or her employer without notice where the employee or the
-- src:1003 | employee’s dependant is immediately threatened by danger to the
-- src:1004 | person by violence or disease that the employee did not by his or her
-- src:1005 | contract of service undertake to run.
@ref s 15 (src:1001-1005)
GIVEN `the employee is the person threatened` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person threatened is the employee's dependant` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the danger is immediate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the danger is to the person by violence or disease` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee undertook by the contract of service to run the danger` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15 the employee may terminate the contract of service without notice` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "immediately threatened by danger to the person by violence or disease that the employee did not by his or her contract of service undertake to run" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): the danger is not immediate, is not danger to the person by violence or disease, or is one the employee undertook to run
        IF (NOT `the danger is immediate`) OR (NOT `the danger is to the person by violence or disease`) OR `the employee undertook by the contract of service to run the danger` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person threatened is a dependant comes from the definition of "dependant", which may give none
        IF (NOT `the employee is the person threatened`) AND (`the person threatened is the employee's dependant` EQUALS NOTHING) THEN NOTHING
        IF `the employee is the person threatened` OR (`the person threatened is the employee's dependant` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the employee or the employee’s dependant is immediately threatened" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): the person threatened is neither the employee nor a dependant
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 16 Liability on breach of contract`

-- "Subject to anything in the contract of service to the contrary": the liability is
-- the sum of section 11, had the party terminated without notice.  Where the party
-- gave notice that was insufficient the Act does not say whether the sum is for the
-- whole period or for the shortfall, so only the no-notice case is answered.
-- src:1009 | 16. Subject to anything in the contract of service to the contrary, the
-- src:1010 | party who breaks the contract of service is liable to pay to the other
-- src:1011 | party a sum equal to the amount the firstmentioned party would have
-- src:1012 | been liable to pay under section 11 had the firstmentioned party
-- src:1013 | terminated the contract of service without notice or with insufficient
-- src:1014 | notice.
@ref s 16 (src:1009-1014)
GIVEN `the party broke the contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contract of service provides to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16 the party who breaks the contract of service is liable to pay the other party the sum` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to anything in the contract of service to the contrary"
        IF `the contract of service provides to the contrary` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the party broke the contract of service` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 16 speaks only of "the party who breaks the contract of service"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 16 (src:1009-1014)
GIVEN `the party terminated without notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum under section 11(1)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 16 the sum the party is liable to pay` MEANS
    IF `the party terminated without notice`
    THEN `the sum under section 11(1)`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "had the firstmentioned party terminated the contract of service without notice or with insufficient notice" -- the Act does not say whether the sum for insufficient notice is for the whole period or for the shortfall
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 17 Contract of service not to restrict rights of employees to join, participate in or organise trade unions`

DECLARE `s 17 Right of the employee` IS ONE OF
    `s 17(a) the right to join a registered trade union`
    `s 17(b) the right to participate in the activities of a registered trade union, whether as an officer of the trade union or otherwise`
    `s 17(c) the right to associate with any other persons for the purpose of organising a trade union in accordance with the provisions of the Trade Unions Act 1940`
    `s 17 a right that the section does not name`

-- src:1019 | 17. Subject to any other written law for the time being in force,
-- src:1020 | nothing in any contract of service restricts, in any way, the right of
-- src:1021 | any employee who is a party to such contract —
-- src:1023 | (a) to join a registered trade union;
-- src:1025 | (b) to participate in the activities of a registered trade union,
-- src:1026 | whether as an officer of the trade union or otherwise; or
-- src:1028 | (c) to associate with any other persons for the purpose of
-- src:1029 | organising a trade union in accordance with the provisions
-- src:1030 | of the Trade Unions Act 1940.
@ref s 17 (src:1019-1030)
GIVEN right IS A `s 17 Right of the employee`
      `another written law for the time being in force restricts the right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 a term of the contract of service restricts the right of the employee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section names three rights and says nothing of any other
        IF (right EQUALS `s 17 a right that the section does not name`) THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to any other written law for the time being in force"
        IF `another written law for the time being in force restricts the right` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in any contract of service restricts, in any way, the right of any employee who is a party to such contract" -- marginal (a)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
